{
  "id": "07-what-did-it-grow",
  "title": "What Did It Grow?",
  "tenet": "Bear fruit",
  "durationMs": 69612,
  "text": "Imagine a boy proudly showing his aunt a patch of ground he has cleared. There is not a weed in sight. \"You worked hard,\" she says. \"What will you plant?\" He has not thought about that. Across the path, his sister is picking tomatoes from a bed she has tended for weeks. Later, she fills a small bowl and takes it to their neighbour. The boy looks back at his clean, empty patch. Tomorrow, he decides, he will begin planting.\n\nBear fruit. Removing what harms us prepares the ground for something good to grow. Spiritual maturity becomes visible in love: food for someone who is hungry, company for someone who is lonely, forgiveness, patient work, and gifts put to use. A clear field is a beginning. Keep planting, watering, and tending. You may not see the harvest immediately. Continue anyway. The fruit is the good that reaches others because you kept walking with God.\n\nAsk yourself: who could be helped by what God has placed in my hands? Choose one person and one action. Take that step today. Plant something good in the garden each day.",
